ITEM A. BUILD KS-1822 (branch `feature/ks-1822-<slug>`, one PR, Refs KS-1822, never Closes).
The fix, spelled out:
1. A NEW file `anchoring/src/anchorReadGate.ts` (do not edit `anchorOverwriteGuard.ts`; import `readIdOwners` and `isUuidShaped` from it). One exported async function, for example `mayReadAnchorRows(documentIds, caller, log)`, with the write gate's decision table EXACTLY: refuse only when an id is held by a `documents` row whose tenant is not the caller's; allow with a named reason when no document holds the id (Platform S's flat anchors), when every id resolves to the caller's own tenant, when the caller has no usable tenant claim (not uuid-shaped), and when the probe faults (fail-open, logged at warn). Compare tenants with the same `sameUuid` semantics (case-insensitive uuid).
2. Two call sites in `index.ts`, one per handler, each a SINGLE `await` plus an early return, placed as the first statement after the rows are fetched (for `:id`: after `anchor` is resolved on both the anchor-id path and the document-id fallback path, so the fallback is gated too; for `/document/:documentId`: after `dbResults`). Add one import line. Touch nothing else in `index.ts`.
3. On refusal the response is the SAME 404 (status AND body, byte for byte) that the route already returns for an absent row, never a 403 (the write path's 403 names a refusal; a read refusal that differs from "absent" is an existence oracle, and the H2 comment at `index.ts:971-982` already rules out id reflection). The server log names the document id and both tenants; the response never does. THIS IS THE ONE CHOICE I MADE FOR WEDNESDAY AND KAM; it is stated again in your READY mail.
4. NAMED RESIDUALS the fix deliberately leaves, to be written in the PR body and the ticket comment as "Known gaps", not hidden: (i) a flat anchor whose `document_id` names no document stays readable by any authenticated caller (the row records no owner; needs KS-1384's tenant column); (ii) a caller with no usable tenant claim stays allowed (the same hole as KS-1652); (iii) a probe fault stays allowed (inherited fail-open; whether reads should fail closed is a question for Kam, put it in the READY mail as one line, not a blocker); (iv) two organisations inside one tenant are not separated (KS-1384 per-organisation rule; KS-1695 and KS-1663 are the neighbouring tickets); (v) `GET /api/anchors/thread-state/:documentId` (`index.ts:1103`), `GET /api/anchors/tx/:txHash` (`:1159`) and `GET /api/anchors/queue` (`:1297`) have 0 tenant/user/caller/organi hits in their line ranges by my search, and I did NOT read their bodies: REPORT them in the mail as candidate same-shape findings; do not extend this PR to them and do not file anything.

